</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Bove</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Wearing</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bachman</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooney</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The clinical epidemiology of crime victimization in older adults: a multidisciplinary pilot study</article-title><source>J Elder Abuse Neglect</source><year>2001</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>79</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1300/J084v13n03_05</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</collab></person-group><article-title>Neighborhood safety and the prevalence of physical inactivity &#x02013; selected states 1996</article-title><source>MMWR Weekly</source><year>1999</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>143</fpage><lpage>146</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neighborhood and individual factors in activity in older adults: results from the neighborhood and senior health study</article-title><source>J Aging Phys Act</source><year>2008</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>144</fpage><lpage>170</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18483439</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Robert</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>LW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Age variation in the relationship between community socioeconomic status and adult health</article-title><source>Research on Aging</source><year>2001</year><volu